theory.intro:
A **polynomial** is an expression made by adding and subtracting terms of the form $ax^{n}$, where every index $n$ is a whole number. Words like **degree**, **leading term** and **monic** describe its parts.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\node[anchor=west] (lhs) at (0,0) {$P(x)=$};
\node[anchor=base west, inner sep=0pt] (coef) at (lhs.base east) {$a_{n}$};
\node[anchor=base west, inner sep=0pt] (xbase) at (coef.base east) {$x$};
\node[anchor=base west, inner sep=0pt, font=\small] (degree) at ([yshift=0.7ex]xbase.base east) {$n$};
\node[anchor=base west] (mid) at ([yshift=-0.7ex]degree.base east) {$+a_{n-1}x^{n-1}+\cdots+a_{1}x+$};
\node[anchor=base west, draw=black, rounded corners, inner sep=2pt] (ct) at (mid.base east) {$a_{0}$};
\node[black, font=\small, align=center, anchor=south] (LC) at ([yshift=1.2cm]coef.north) {Leading\\coefficient};
\node[black, font=\small, align=center, anchor=south] (DG) at ([xshift=2.2cm,yshift=1.2cm]degree.north) {Degree\\(highest index)};
\node[black, font=\small, anchor=north] (LT) at ([yshift=-1.0cm]xbase.south west) {Leading term};
\node[black, font=\small, anchor=north] (CN) at ([yshift=-1.0cm]ct.south) {Constant term};
\draw[black] ([yshift=-0.15cm]coef.south west) -- ([yshift=-0.3cm]coef.south west) -- ([yshift=-0.3cm]degree.south east) -- ([yshift=-0.15cm]degree.south east);
\draw[black,->] (LC.south) -- (coef.north);
\draw[black,->] (DG.south west) -- (degree.north);
\draw[black,->] (LT.north) -- ([yshift=-0.3cm]xbase.south west);
\draw[black,->] (CN.north) -- (ct.south);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
